diff --git a/tests/host/vm-query-fastpath/README.md b/tests/host/vm-query-fastpath/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..c548ba01ea2874861758cfcd59f13a1e791dbaf1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/host/vm-query-fastpath/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+# Actual-source VM query differential
+
+`python3 check.py SOURCE OUTPUT` compiles the production lookup, protection
+decoder and query against the frozen prior production functions for both actual
+32-bit ABI arithmetic (`-m32`, including the 28-byte MBI) and the 64-bit host
+model (`-m64`). A multilib C compiler and both ABIs' ASan/UBSan libraries are
+required; the supported `spiritboot-toolchain` Docker image supplies them.
+38,160 cases per ABI compare full output bytes/status/guards, mutex checks and
+explicit work budgets across sparse/mixed PDE/PTE spans and zero/one/16/256
+region lists. The 99 additional main compatibility cases cover a wrapped high
+tail, final-PDE rounding and the overlapping list left by an accepted wrapped
+release, with adjacent ends and address bounds. A PDE-probe budget bounds the
+cycle regression, and each executable also has a 60-second timeout.
+`--allow-baseline` runs the same semantic comparison before the patch; without
+that option the old implementation fails the intended one-list-walk assertion.
+`--abi 32` or `--abi 64` selects one build; `--scenario tail-wrap`, `pde-wrap` or
+`release-wrap` selects a regression. The public native fixture independently
+checks the target ABI. Neither fixture reads proprietary implementation code.
diff --git a/tests/host/vm-query-fastpath/baseline-query.c b/tests/host/vm-query-fastpath/baseline-query.c
